hello there how many languages do you  speak  es  espanol  palettes  you know  all too often in the anglo-saxon world  the answer is i speak one language i  think that's rather unfortunate  i think people today  can and should speak three or four or  more languages  you know the languages of the world are  divided into  families of languages but two families  account for about two-thirds  of all the language speakers in the  world  the largest group is the indo-european  language group that has about 45 percent  of the people in the world and the  saino tibetan which includes chinese  group has another 22 percent so that's a  lot and in my experience if you can  start learning one language in a family  or better still one in each of those two  families you have a good chance of  learning other languages of that family  and that's been my experience i made an  investment  in french and then in chinese mandarin  chinese when i was in my late teens and  early 20s and from that base i've been  able to learn  right now a total of 10 languages and i  haven't stopped i intend to continue  and one major reason why i want to  continue  is that language learning is one of the  most useful self-improvement activities  that you can undertake  research has shown that language  learning is very very good for brain  fitness for your memory  for staving off  alzheimer's  you're constantly forced to create new  patterns in your brain as you struggle  to get used to new languages  but language learning should be a  pleasant activity  all too often  in our schools language learning is made  to be an unpleasant activity people  dislike learning french in school or  whatever other language they have to  learn but that's not how i learn  languages and i talk about that at my  blog thelinguist.blogs.com  when i learn i just do pleasant things  because the more pleasant the  association i have with the language the  better i learn so i listen i read  i've even developed a system for  learning words and phrases and for  associating pleasant thoughts and  pleasing context with those words and  phrases and i talk about this at my blog  but the main thing is you have to have  an attitude  of  wanting to enjoy the language believing  that you can do it  accepting the language and you'll be  surprised at how well you can learn and  the benefits are enormous  i know there are people who are involved  in pilates and yoga  and mountain climbing and all other  kinds of activities  that they hope will improve their mind  and their body  and that's all well and good  but i would vote for language learning  as being the most beneficial activity  that you can engage in because not only  do you end up with an increased ability  to communicate with your fellow human  beings you also train your brain  and the whole experience can be  extremely enjoyable if it's done the  right way so once again this is steve  kaufman here  i hope to see you at my blog  thelinguist.blogs.com  now let's see we can say audra adios  and  it's not just a matter of showing off  with a few phrases it's a matter of  enjoying the fact that you can  communicate comfortably with people of a  different culture and i have done that  for much of my life traveling to  different countries and it has helped me  not only socially but also in my  business so once again  why don't you come to visit my blog and  also take the plunge and learn another  language
 

